# Planted bugs in the three-step inductive proof. Each one must make its
# property fail.
run fv-apalache Lease.tla Init.icfg Step.icfg Safety.icfg
properties StrongInv Safety
file Lease.tla

mutation Acquire no longer checks that the slot is free
detects StrongInv
-     /\ phase = "idle"
-     /\ leases' = leases + 1
+     /\ leases' = leases + 1

mutation Init starts with a lease already outstanding
detects StrongInv
- Init == leases = 0 /\ phase = "idle"
+ Init == leases = 1 /\ phase = "idle"

mutation Safety is stated more strictly than StrongInv guarantees
detects Safety
- Safety == leases <= 1
+ Safety == leases <= 0

harmless a comment on the inductive invariant
- StrongInv == (phase = "idle" /\ leases = 0) \/ (phase = "held" /\ leases = 1)
+ StrongInv == (phase = "idle" /\ leases = 0) \/ (phase = "held" /\ leases = 1)  \* the two fields agree
